{
  "what": "The whole of the control board card file /sd/config.txt, reconstructed key by key, and compared with the firmware shipped default.",
  "why": [
    "The file itself cannot be read: the console `cat` answers `File not found` for every path on this build (bench B7), and no download path is implemented (Z1-Bridge-Protocol.md 5, 9).",
    "`config-get sd <key>` is the only channel that answers, and it answers one key at a time, so the file is reconstructed rather than fetched.",
    "A key ABSENT from this file is not unset: it falls through to the firmware compiled-in default, and the `firm` source that would give that is answered with silence.",
    "Comparing against configZ1.default turns `what does the file say` into `what did the vendor change`."
  ],
